/* book exam traps: Adding the four cut readings (56.6 kW) instead of the four drops. A cut reading still contains the brake power of the other cylinders. | Reporting a negative friction power. FP is small and positive; a negative value means a cut reading was copied wrongly or BP was noted with the wrong number of cylinders firing. | Using N instead of N/2 in the indicated power formula for a four-stroke. That doubles IP, so the efficiency you calculate is half the true value: the 85.5 % example would come out near 43 %. | Mixing units in IP = imep × Vd × N/(60 nR). Use kPa with m³, or convert bar to kPa (×100) and litres to m³ (×10⁻³). */
